// Respawn: a Reanimate-carrying player against ordinary wild programs.
//
// The player's own cast never fires here — `model: Tactical` in the bin
// drives every party body through `PartyTurns::SwingOnly` (see the
// README's "What the `arena` bin does not measure"), so `character.routine`
// only proves the fixture stages a Respawn-equipped player without an
// error. The mechanism this file actually exercises is the **hostile**
// side: `respawn.ron`'s `wild_weight: 4` means any wild spawn here may roll
// it onto its own `Routines`, and a wild carrier *is* driven by the same
// `tactical/ai.rs` a played fight uses, routine invocations included. A
// pair over 50 reps gives enough spawns and enough falls (bodies killed and
// re-raised, both sides' reap and dissolve paths, a raised body's own
// further death) to turn up a carrier casting it somewhere in the run
// without depending on any one seed's luck.
//
// `cargo run --bin arena -- dev-arenas/respawn.ron` — the check is that it
// finishes with no panic, not a particular win rate.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 6, zone: 2),
    character: (routine: Some("respawn")),
    opponents: [(species: "sub_process", count: 2)],
    model: Tactical,
    approach: Some(East),
    reps: 50,
    seed: 5,
)
